NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: Largely NAMING, not mechanism. The packet's claimed delta is 'AGENT-inter-turn-gap-timed' proactive demote+prefetch vs 'reactive-on-preemption' / 'speculative-token' / 'cross-request reuse'. But AttentionStore/CachedAttention and Pensieve ALREADY time KV save/restore to the CONVERSATION-turn gap with overlap. An agent tool-call inter-turn gap is mechanistically a conversation-turn gap (idle wall-time between a session's consecutive turns). 'Agent' vs 'chat' is a domain re-skin of the same demote-on-turn-end / prefetch-on-turn-start / overlap-with-idle loop. The genuine mechanism residue — if any — is (a) using the KNOWN/predictable agent-gap DISTRIBUTION (tool-latency tail) to schedule/admit prefetch under PCIe contention, and (b) the contention-aware win/kill boundary C/p_rr*bytes > B_total*gap. (b) is a measurement contribution, not a new mechanism; (a) is a plausible-but-unproven delta over AttentionStore's overlap scheduling.

